    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e20bfca_d569ea4a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001405
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-15T11:34:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "C TFA supports that: https://trustedfirmware-a.readthedocs.io/en/latest/design/firmware-design.html#cpu-specific-reset-handling\n\nright now RFA has only cpu-specific reset handlers, platforms may need to perform some additional platform, but usually not core, specific setup.",
      "parentUuid": "4e0dc45b_6ab089a8",
      "revId": "a2c0b770945c9c4acd9c7225e939fcbb65491b52",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc92f4b4_6e5171cb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000309
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-15T16:59:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, but do you have a specific use-case in mind? If it\u0027s for platform-specific errata then shouldn\u0027t that be handled by the errata framework?",
      "parentUuid": "8e20bfca_d569ea4a",
      "revId": "a2c0b770945c9c4acd9c7225e939fcbb65491b52",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5849ac41_789ceff7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001405
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-16T08:58:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that erratas are meant to fix hardware bugs, while platform specific reset handlers make it possible to e.g. configure ACTLR_EL3",
      "parentUuid": "dc92f4b4_6e5171cb",
      "revId": "a2c0b770945c9c4acd9c7225e939fcbb65491b52",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f9c490b_61546591",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000309
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-16T10:45:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that errata are about hardware bugs.\n\nIs there a reason why `ACTLR_EL3` can\u0027t be configured from Rust code? It looks like it just controls lower-EL access to features, so it shouldn\u0027t need to be configured so early in the reset flow.",
      "parentUuid": "5849ac41_789ceff7",
      "revId": "a2c0b770945c9c4acd9c7225e939fcbb65491b52",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c28b7d55_2c5f2701",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001405
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-16T11:13:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "good point. probably `actlr_el3` can be configured later. However, I\u0027m not sure if we can configure `CLUSTERECTLR` (DSU / cache setup) from Rust code:\n\nhttps://developer.arm.com/documentation/100453/0401/Control-registers/CLUSTERECTLR--Cluster-Extended-Control-Register\n\n\"It must only be written to as part of the initial system configuration setup following reset\"",
      "parentUuid": "6f9c490b_61546591",
      "revId": "a2c0b770945c9c4acd9c7225e939fcbb65491b52",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "958fbe8d_56323d50",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000309
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-16T12:41:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like C TF-A currently has only one platform upstream which sets `CLUSTERECTLR_EL1`. This does so from C code, see `setup_clusterectlr_el1` in the agilex5 platform. As far as I can see this is only called on the primary CPU core. Whether this is correct I don\u0027t know, but if it is then the same should be possible in Rust.",
      "parentUuid": "c28b7d55_2c5f2701",
      "revId": "a2c0b770945c9c4acd9c7225e939fcbb65491b52",
      "serverId": "8f6f209b-db1a-4cbf-aa44-c8bc30e9bfda"
    },
